<title>MEXICO: Mexico reopens crude ports as weather improves.</title>
<headline>Mexico reopens crude ports as weather improves.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Transportation and Communications Ministry said Wednesday that two crucial crude oil ports in the Gulf of Mexico were reopened earlier in the day as local weather conditions improved.</p>
<p>In an update, the ministry said both Pajaritos and Dos Bocas ports were reopened to shipping. Both had been closed since late Sunday because of bad weather whipped up by Hurricane Josephine.</p>
<p>Mexico's third crude port in the Gulf -- Cayo Arcos -- was never shut to shipping.</p>
<p>The only port still closed in the Gulf is Frontera in Tabasco state, the ministry added.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
